# .trivyignore — accepted / triaged Trivy findings for evc-mesh
#
# The trivy CI gate (.github/workflows/trivy.yml) runs `trivy fs` over the repo
# and fails the build on any CRITICAL or HIGH dependency vulnerability that HAS
# a fix available (ignore-unfixed: true).
#
# Add a CVE here ONLY after a deliberate accept-risk decision, and ALWAYS
# document it inline: CVE → why it is not actionable/exploitable for us →
# who accepted it → date. Revisit on each dependency bump.
#
# Format (one finding ID per line):
#   # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN — <reason not exploitable / no adoptable fix>. Accepted by <name> <date>.
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#
# A line here outlives whatever made it necessary. CVE-2026-32285 was accepted
# 2026-05-23 pending a deploy-gated bump; Dependabot shipped the same bump 15
# minutes later (#123) and the dependency left the tree entirely on 2026-07-08
# (#257) — the suppression stayed for 68 days, silently disarmed for a CVE that
# would have muzzled trivy had the dependency ever come back transitively.
# So the trivy job now fails if any ID below matches nothing trivy can see:
# see the "stale .trivyignore entries" step in .github/workflows/trivy.yml.
